Hi Perry, thanks a lot! It’s much clearer now and very useful to see how to allow the ode call to reference cmodel. On a related note it would be great if nimble had ode functionality, and not just to be able to use in a BUGS model, but more generally to allow an ode system to be compiled via nimble then called by lsoda or whatever. I had a quick look at trying to pass a compiled nimble function to deSolve but the prototype is different (it expects an R list return value among other things and so did not seem trivial). The current compiled function route in deSolve via C functions is quite a lot of fiddly work but can make a huge difference in performance, especially for solving PDEs which need many calls to the solver. Best wishes. Fraser.

